emocracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-24","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Concurrent Meeting of the Thriving People and Thriving Council Committees","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Fuel costs 31% higher than prior year; multiple concurrent cost pressures emerging","lead":"Multiple concurrent cost pressures indicate the council is absorbing inflation across multiple budget lines, reducing budget flexibility; if energy or labour costs accelerate further, buffers may be limited.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Significant aged debt outstanding: \u00a30.206m overdue by 90+ days, with 86% over 150 days old","lead":"Aged debt indicates cash collection difficulties and working capital strain; extended overdue periods suggest either weak debtor creditworthiness or collection process issues, affecting liquidity forecasting.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Wellbeing Lincs Responder Service contract delivering half expected income; ongoing pressure forecast","lead":"A contracted income source missing half its target signals demand forecasting problems or service viability issues, raising questions about income budget reliability and the council's ability to predict contracted outcomes.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","headline":"Fuel costs 31% higher than prior year; multiple concurrent cost pressures emerging","detail":"Fuel costs are averaging \u00a31.40 per litre in 2026-27 vs \u00a31.07 in 2025-26, creating a \u00a30.068m budget pressure. Combined with parish lighting electricity and maintenance pressures (\u00a30.021m) and a \u00a30.007m pay award pressure (after vacancy offsets), multiple cost lines are under pressure simultaneously. The council reports these are currently contained within budget but represent emerging inflation risk.","category":"overspend","matters":"Multiple concurrent cost pressures indicate the council is absorbing inflation across multiple budget lines, reducing budget flexibility; if energy or labour costs accelerate further, buffers may be limited.","figures":"Fuel pressure \u00a30.068m; parish lighting \u00a30.021m; pay pressure \u00a30.007m (contained but forecast)","quote":"There is a forecast pressure against fuel budgets of \u00a30.068m. The average fuel price to date is \u00a31.40 per litre, with an average price of \u00a31.36 per litre forecast for the remainder of the year (compared to the average price paid per litre during 2025/2026 of \u00a31.07).","material":false},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","headline":"Significant aged debt outstanding: \u00a30.206m overdue by 90+ days, with 86% over 150 days old","detail":"As of 31 May 2026, sundry debtor aged debt totals \u00a30.206m, with \u00a30.177m (86%) overdue by more than 150 days. Main contributors are Housing (\u00a30.065m), Property Services (\u00a30.062m), Environmental Services (\u00a30.033m), and others. The council notes debt recovery processes are underway.","category":"income","matters":"Aged debt indicates cash collection difficulties and working capital strain; extended overdue periods suggest either weak debtor creditworthiness or collection process issues, affecting liquidity forecasting.","figures":"\u00a30.206m total aged debt (90+ days); \u00a30.177m over 150 days old (86% of total)","quote":"At the end of May 2026, there was a total of \u00a30.206m outstanding debt in the system over 90 days. Much of this debt was over 150 days old (86%)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","headline":"Wellbeing Lincs Responder Service contract delivering half expected income; ongoing pressure forecast","detail":"The contract with East Lindsey District Council was budgeted to contribute \u00a30.077m annually. After a full year of operation in 2025-26, it delivered only \u00a30.039m\u2014a shortfall of \u00a30.038m (49%). For 2026-27, a further pressure of \u00a30.035m is forecast. The paper states this ongoing impact will be reviewed ahead of budget setting for 2027-28.","category":"income","matters":"A contracted income source missing half its target signals demand forecasting problems or service viability issues, raising questions about income budget reliability and the council's ability to predict contracted outcomes.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a30.077m; actual 2025-26 \u00a30.039m (shortfall \u00a30.038m, 49% miss); 2026-27 pressure \u00a30.035m","quote":"Initial estimates of the impact of the contract on the bottom line for the Council were a contribution of \u00a30.077m. Following a full year of the service being operational the actual contribution for 2025/2026 was \u00a30.039m \u2013 a shortfall of \u00a30.038m. A pressure of \u00a30.035m is forecast for 2026/2027.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Thriving Council Committee","paper_title":"FINAL Budget and Treasury Monitoring - Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52143/52143.pdf","headline":"General Fund Balance forecast to drop below agreed minimum working balance requirement","detail":"The council's General Fund Balance is forecast to be \u00a31.985m as of 31 March 2027, falling below the minimum working balance range of \u00a32.0m-\u00a32.5m that members have agreed. The council notes this includes the \u00a30.073m revenue deficit at Q1. Any balance remaining below \u00a32.0m would be funded from the Budget Stability Reserve, using contingency resources to cover the shortfall.","category":"reserves","matters":"A council falling below its minimum working balance has reduced financial resilience for unplanned costs or revenue shocks\u2014a key indicator of financial stress for lenders assessing liquidity and operational flexibility.","figures":"\u00a31.985m forecast vs \u00a32.0m-\u00a32.5m agreed minimum range; deficit of \u00a30.073m at Q1","quote":"The forecast General Fund Balance as of 31st March 2027 is \u00a31.985m (excluding carry forwards). This is outside of the range of the minimum working balance agreed by Members of between \u00a32.0m and \u00a32.5m","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-21","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 Internal Audit Follow up report","paper_url":"https://democracy.west-lindsey.gov.uk/documents/s52044/52044.pdf","headline":"Overall audit follow-up shows only 44% completion rate, with auditors concluding the council has demonstrated 'little progress' on implementing management actions","detail":"Of 18 management actions due for implementation by 28 February 2026, only 8 (44%) were fully implemented or superseded. Five actions (28%) were partially implemented and four (22%) were not implemented at all. The auditors' formal assessment is that the council has demonstrated 'little progress' in implementing agreed actions.","category":"governance","matters":"Slow follow-through on audit recommendations suggests weak governance culture and difficulty translating audit findings into operational change. This affects how quickly and effectively the council responds to control weaknesses.","figures":"9 of 18 actions confirmed as completed or no longer necessary (50%); 5 actions partially implemented (28%); 4 actions not implemented (22%)","quote":"Of the actions considered, testing found that nine actions had been implemented or superseded, five actions were partially implemented, and the remaining four actions were not implemented.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-30"},"name":"West Lindsey","findings_total":51,"news_drafts_total":3}}